  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want a tap on a section title in Favoris (e.g. « Apple ») to open that category's topic list, as legacy does, instead of **freezing the app**.\n\n### Observed (operator, iPhone, 2026-11-16, current dense rows plus « Mode compact » on)\n\n- Favoris tab, sectioned by category. A tap on a section title such as « Apple » does **not** open the category's topic list, and the **app freezes**.\n- Steps: Réglages › Mode compact on, Favoris triés par catégories on; Favoris tab; tap « Apple ».\n\n### Code path (read, not reproduced)\n\n- The header button calls `openCategory(source)` (`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicListView.swift:228-230`).\n- That reaches `NavigationModel.openCategory` (`NavigationModel.swift:97-100`), which sets `topicFilter?.flag = .favorites`: it **also writes the global choice**, as legacy `Favorites.swift:357` @ 87fe0d1c does. It then sets `openedCategory` to push the list on the Favoris stack.\n- Hypothesis to verify, not a conclusion: the global filter write makes the Favoris list re-evaluate or reload while the push is in flight. That gives a SwiftUI update loop or a main-thread wait, possibly only with compact density (`densityHeaderMargin`) or when the filter already equals `.favorites`.\n\n### Expected\n\nThe category's topic list is pushed on the Favoris stack, with the Favoris filter, as legacy does. No freeze, in compact or regular density, sectioned or not. On a regular-width iPad, `RootModel.showCategoryFromFavorites` switches to Catégories.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The root cause is named with evidence: a hosted test, or a main-thread hang captured in a test.\n- [ ] A test that drives `openCategory` from the Favoris section header, with compact density on, fails (hangs or does not push) without the fix and passes with it.\n- [ ] Device check in the general review.\n\n### Blocked by\n- a Mac Instruments trace (Hangs or Time Profiler, main thread) of the freeze on the device or the iOS 27 simulator: Favoris tab, compact density, sectioned list, tap on a section title (e.g. « Apple »). The hosted test of #990 did not reproduce it (run 44009600569: `openCategory` pushes in 1.9 s).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
